//- components/_focus.pug
//- One Focus entry within a skill's Focus list: a checkbox marking whether
//- the player has learned that focus, plus an action button that rolls a
//- 2d20 test for skill+this focus (see initiateFocusRoll in
//- views/_character.pug's +module block). A plain +action is used rather
//- than +roller, since a roller's visible button is a native Roll20
//- "roll"-type button that Roll20 handles itself on click (using its own
//- default chat template) rather than reliably invoking our sheetworker.
mixin focusItem(skillName, focusName)
  - const slug = focusName.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, ' ').trim();
  span.cc-focus-item
    +checkbox({name: `${skillName} focus ${slug} known`}).cc-focus-checkbox
    +action({
      name: `${skillName} focus ${slug} roll`,
      class: 'cc-focus-roll roller',
      trigger: {triggeredFuncs: ['initiateFocusRoll']}
    })
      = focusName
